---
description: Reminder for actions that must happen in the Unity Editor UI, not by editing files
alwaysApply: false
---

Some operations can't or shouldn't be done by hand-editing files: creating Sprite Atlases,
setting up Animator state machines, assigning Inspector references that depend on a
stable GUID, baking lighting/NavMesh, importing Asset Store packages.

Don't hand-write the resulting .meta/.asset YAML from scratch for these. Do: give me exact
click-by-click Editor steps, and write any C#/Shader Graph logic that depends on the
result assuming it will exist after I do the manual step.
